  "slug": "japan-meeting-of-furries",
  "name": "Japan Meeting of Furries",
  "shortName": "JMF",
  "description": "The Japan Meeting of Furries (JMoF) is an annual furry convention in Japan, founded in 2012 to establish the first hotel-based furry convention in the country. The first was held January 12 to 14, 2013, in Hikone, Shiga, and it was held for many years at the Loisir Hotel in Toyohashi, Aichi, before moving to Tokoname, and it will move to Aichi Sky Expo from 2027. Programming includes workshops and seminars on acting, costume-building and art. Since 2020 it has also run a parallel online convention in virtual worlds, with panels livestreamed and chances for virtual and physical attendees to interact. Its charity is the Toyohashi Zoo Botanical Park, and attendance has grown from 100 to over 2,500, the largest in Asia.",
